  "endpoint_domain": "Plan instances only using the full Atom/(.Header.Role: Plan)// selector in both written directions. Relation-object signatures have no cardinalities.",
  "endpoint_permissions_required": [
    "CA-R-2511 preview explicitly permits 0+ outgoing IS_BLOCKED_BY and 0+ outgoing derived BLOCKS for Plan instances. The 0+ allowance admits optional/multiple prerequisites and requires none; it does not create links.",
    "Check dynamic Relation representation against the selected CA-R-2709 and CA-D-657 authority; D471 preview specifies the direct key, IDs and sequence but does not by itself establish runtime/schema support."
  ],
  "integration_gates": [
    "Apply the six reviewed current/new source proposals as one coordinated source packet after full validation, allocation and frozen-reference checks.",
    "The D471 direct storage encoding replaces existing relations.blocks on the prerequisite with relations.IS_BLOCKED_BY on the dependent. Data, fixture and code migration, including collision handling and exact old-to-new orientation, belongs to CA #3; this packet changes none.",
    "Merge the CA-M-306 proposal with the separately owned confidence-retry WIP before any source application, and preserve any later accepted changes.",
    "Review Current CA-E-504, CA-E-404, CA-E-622, CA-M-239 and CA-R-1592 consumers as logical BLOCKS views; keep their semantics unless they explicitly author or treat the derived view as a stored fact.",
    "Validate nested-key admission and representation against CA-R-2709 and CA-D-657; do not infer runtime support or create an unapproved Property.",
    "Recheck all exact live source and candidate pins and archive exact predecessors under the authorized workflow."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Relation signature and Plan permissions are source proposals only; actual Plan data/code/fixture migration is owned by CA #3.",
    "No canonical source, code, tests, Git or actual Plan instance was changed.",
    "CA-M-306 scope/assignee/author/retry assumptions were removed rather than replaced by invented Properties; other Current Rules still govern completion and source resolution."
  ]
}
